  "conclusion": "Nested cross-validation chose thresholds from 0.087 to 0.163. On the locked folds they caught all 224 High records with 163 false alarms: cost $8,150 against $57,950 for the default rule (-85.9%), flag rate 7.74%. The in-sample best ($7,950 at 0.112) is only $200 lower, so the selection optimism is small here. High F1 falls from 0.815 to 0.733, because the cost rule accepts false alarms to remove misses. Perfect recall reflects clean synthetic data with oracle-informed features. These are cross-validation estimates; test-1000.csv is untouched."
